{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-isic-4290"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Construction of Other Civil Engineering Projects"
 :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev5 "4290"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :construction/other-civil-engineering
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:worker-safety :buried-utility-strike-prevention :excavation-collapse-prevention]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :civilworks-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics false
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:identity :forms :audit-ledger :notifications]
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "`:civilworks-governor` is implemented end-to-end in `src/civilworks` as
 an OTHER-CIVIL-ENGINEERING-PROJECT OPERATIONS COORDINATION actor -- Civil
 Works Advisor (LLM proposal-only) ⊣ Civil Works Governor (closed-op-
 allowlist / site-and-permit-verification / pre-work buried-utility-
 survey / excavation-shoring / unresolved-concern hard-gates).
 Deliberately narrower in authority than the `cloud-itonami-isic-4211`
 (community building construction) robotics-premise reference this actor
 follows structurally, and structured after the sibling
 `cloud-itonami-isic-4329` (other construction installation) and
 `cloud-itonami-isic-4390` (other specialized construction activities)
 coordination-only actors: `:itonami.blueprint/robotics` is honestly
 `false` here -- this actor holds NO heavy-equipment-control authority and
 NO structural-completion-sign-off authority (both are HARD, permanent
 governor blocks, never overridable by human approval -- see
 `civilworks.governor` ns docstring). Every one of its four proposal ops
 (`:log-site-record` / `:schedule-construction-operation` / `:flag-
 safety-concern` / `:order-supplies`) carries `:effect :propose` ONLY --
 the governor HARD-holds any proposal that doesn't
 (`effect-not-propose-violations`), a structural invariant distinguishing
 this actor from siblings that DO commit real-world actuation effects.
 Covers the RESIDUAL civil-engineering category -- construction of
 industrial plants (process/manufacturing-facility civil works),
 pipelines (long-distance and local, excluding the utility-network
 projects `cloud-itonami-isic-4220` already covers), power-line/electric-
 transmission-line construction, and outdoor sports facilities (running
 tracks, sports fields, playgrounds) -- work not elsewhere classified in
 ISIC division 42 (distinct from `cloud-itonami-isic-4211`/`4212`
 buildings/roads-and-railways and `cloud-itonami-isic-4220` utility-
 network projects, both already `:implemented` in this fleet).
 Per-jurisdiction pre-work buried-utility/ground-condition survey and
 excavation-shoring legal-basis catalog (JPN/USA/DEU, `civilworks.facts`)
 with real official sources (independently verified against
 laws.e-gov.go.jp / osha.gov / dguv.de before being written), and
 mail+phone safety-concern notification (`civilworks.notify`, a portable
 `.cljc` caller-injected transport seam -- no JVM interop, per this
 repo's cljs-first mandate) to the site's supervisor/safety-officer
 contact roster. `:flag-safety-concern` ALWAYS escalates to a human, at
 every phase, unconditionally. Like `cloud-itonami-isic-4329`/
 `cloud-itonami-isic-4390`, `:schedule-construction-operation` here is
 NOT a permanent `high-stakes` member -- it MAY auto-commit at phase 3
 once every HARD check clears and confidence is high (see
 `civilworks.governor`/`civilworks.phase` ns docstrings for the full
 rationale)."}
